{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.LSum","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.polytabloid_mem_specht","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.polytabloid_mem_specht","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L296-L299","doc":"Every polytabloid lies in the Specht module (immediate from the span). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.SpechtSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.SpechtSubmodule","kind":"def","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L290-L294","doc":"The **Specht module** `S^μ ≤ M^μ`: the `k`-submodule spanned by all\npolytabloids.  As a `Submodule.span` it is a submodule **by construction**\n(`sorry`-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.polytabloid","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L282-L288","doc":"The **polytabloid** `e_t = Σ_{π ∈ C_t} sgn(π) · {π • t}` associated to a\ntableau `t`: the signed sum over the column stabilizer of the tabloids of the\ncolumn-permuted tableaux.  This is the canonical spanning vector of the Specht\nmodule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.rep_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.rep_of","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L272-L274","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.rep_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.rep_single","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L267-L270","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.rep","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L252-L265","doc":"The `S_n`-representation on `M^μ`: each `σ` acts by the linear permutation of\nbasis tabloids `domLCongr (Tabloid.mulAction σ)`.  Implemented as a\n`Representation k (Perm (Fin n)) (Mtab μ)` (i.e. a monoid hom into the linear\nautomorphisms), so it is wired for the `MonoidAlgebra k (Perm (Fin n))`-module\nstructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab.of","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L247-L250","doc":"The basis tabloid vector `⟦t⟧ ∈ M^μ` (the `Finsupp.single` at the tabloid of\n`t`, coefficient `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Mtab","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L238-L243","doc":"The **permutation module** `M^μ` = the free `k`-module on tabloids of shape\n`μ`.  The `S_n`-action permutes the basis of tabloids.\n\nMarked `@[reducible]` so the `AddCommGroup`/`Module k` instances on\n`Tabloid μ →₀ k` are transparently inherited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.smul_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.smul_mk","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L231-L232","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.instMulAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.instMulAction","kind":"instance","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L214-L229","doc":"The `S_n`-action descends to tabloids: `σ • {t} = {σ • t}`.  Well-defined\nbecause the action is equivariant for the row pattern (`rowPattern_smul`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.instFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.instFintype","kind":"instance","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L211-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.instDecidableEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.instDecidableEq","kind":"instance","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L208-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid.mk","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L205-L206","doc":"The tabloid of a tableau (its row-equivalence class). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tabloid","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L199-L201","doc":"A **tabloid** `{t}` of shape `μ` is a row-equivalence class of `μ`-tableaux:\nthe data of \"which row each label lives in\", forgetting the order within rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instDecidableRowEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instDecidableRowEquiv","kind":"instance","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L193-L197","doc":"Row-equivalence is decidable (equality of two functions out of a `Fintype`\ninto `ℕ`), which makes the quotient `Tabloid` carry `DecidableEq`/`Fintype`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowEquiv_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowEquiv_iff","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L190-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowEquiv","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L180-L188","doc":"Two tableaux are **row-equivalent** when they have the same row pattern\n(i.e. each label sits in the same row).  This is the setoid whose quotient is the\nset of tabloids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instDecidableMemColStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instDecidableMemColStab","kind":"instance","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L174-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instDecidableMemRowStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instDecidableMemRowStab","kind":"instance","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L167-L172","doc":"Stabilizer membership is decidable (equality of two `Fin n → ℕ` patterns),\nso `rowStab t` / `colStab t` carry a `Fintype` on their underlying subtype — which\nis what makes the polytabloid sum below well-formed without `Set.toFinset` plumbing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.mem_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.mem_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L162-L165","doc":"Membership in the column stabilizer is exactly \"fixes the column pattern\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.mem_rowStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.mem_rowStab","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L157-L160","doc":"Membership in the row stabilizer is exactly \"fixes the row pattern\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.colStab","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L151-L155","doc":"The **column stabilizer** `C_t` of a tableau `t`: the subgroup of `S_n`\npreserving the columns of `t` setwise.  Defined as the `MulAction.stabilizer` of\nthe column pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowStab","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L145-L149","doc":"The **row stabilizer** `R_t` of a tableau `t`: the subgroup of `S_n`\npreserving the rows of `t` setwise.  Defined as the `MulAction.stabilizer` of the\nrow pattern, hence automatically a `Subgroup`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.colPattern_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.colPattern_smul","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L140-L143","doc":"`colPattern` is equivariant: `colPattern (σ • t) = σ • colPattern t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowPattern_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowPattern_smul","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L135-L138","doc":"`rowPattern` is equivariant: `rowPattern (σ • t) = σ • rowPattern t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.arrow_smul_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.arrow_smul_apply","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L131-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instArrowMulAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.instArrowMulAction","kind":"instance","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L119-L129","doc":"The `S_n`-action on label-indexed data `Fin n → ℕ` by relabelling\n(`σ • f = f ∘ σ⁻¹`).  This is the action whose stabilizers are the Young\nrow/column subgroups. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.colPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.colPattern","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L114-L117","doc":"The **column pattern** of a tableau: `colPattern t l` is the column index\n`(t l).1.2` of the cell holding label `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.rowPattern","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L107-L112","doc":"The **row pattern** of a tableau: `rowPattern t l` is the row index `(t l).1.1`\nof the cell holding label `l`.  Two tableaux are row-equivalent iff they have the\nsame row pattern (up to within-row reshuffling), and the row stabilizer is the\nstabilizer of this pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tableau.smul_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tableau.smul_apply","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L99-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tableau.instMulAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tableau.instMulAction","kind":"instance","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L88-L97","doc":"The `S_n`-action on `μ`-tableaux: `σ • t` relabels label `l` to the cell\nthat `t` assigned to `σ⁻¹ l`, i.e. precomposition by `σ⁻¹`.  Concretely\n`(σ • t) = t ∘ σ⁻¹` as an `Equiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.Tableau","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L75-L84","doc":"A **(general) `μ`-tableau** is a bijective filling of the cells of `μ` by the\nlabels `Fin n` (`n = μ.card`).  We carry it as an equivalence `Fin n ≃ μ.cells`:\n`t l` is the cell holding label `l`.  Unlike `StandardYoungTableau` (brick 1)\nthese fillings are **arbitrary** bijections — no monotonicity is imposed.\n\nMarked `@[reducible]` (the standard idiom for a free-construction wrapper) so\nthat `t l`, the `Equiv` operations, and the `Fintype`/`DecidableEq` instances on\n`Fin n ≃ μ.cells` are transparently available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.nOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.nOf","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Specht.lean#L69-L71","doc":"`nOf μ` is the number of cells of `μ`, i.e. the rank of the symmetric group\nacting on tableaux of shape `μ`.  Abbreviation for `μ.card`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}